Article 9 (Restriction of Payments and Prohibition on Use for Other Purposes)
(1) The Director of the National Police Hospital may suspend all or part of the payment of research expenses or recover all or part of research expenses already paid where any of the following applies: Provided, That where a person eligible to receive research expenses under Article 5 falls under subparagraph 4 or 5, the Director shall recover all of the research expenses paid:
1. Where a person applies for payment of research expenses falsely or obtains them by other fraudulent means;
2. Where a person executes research expenses falsely or by other fraudulent means;
3. Where a person who has received research expenses discontinues research due to retirement, transfer, or any other reason: Provided, That expenses already paid need not be recovered where the research has progressed sufficiently for a research report to be submitted by the end of the relevant year;
4. Where a person fails to submit a research report in accordance with the research plan;
5. Where a person uses research expenses for a purpose other than research;
6. Where a researcher fails to faithfully perform duties under Article 7.
(2) Where the Director of the National Police Hospital suspends payment of research expenses or recovers research expenses under paragraph (1), the Director may, following deliberation by the Committee, exclude the person from eligibility to receive research expenses for two years beginning on the first day of the following fiscal year: Provided, That where a recipient under Article 5 falls under paragraph (1) 4 or 5, the Director shall exclude that recipient from eligibility to receive research expenses for two years beginning on the first day of the following fiscal year.
